1
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:24,260
Broke folks, come on over to my place.

2
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:28,960
Not like I've got any, but don't you worry.

3
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:36,040
Look at that, blue sky and white clouds.

4
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:43,160
Mass-production sake ban order

5
00:01:49,060 --> 00:01:50,240
I'm starving.

6
00:01:50,240 --> 00:01:52,900
I haven't eaten a thing since last night.

7
00:01:52,900 --> 00:01:56,000
I've already eaten everything in the fridge,

8
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,300
and there's not even trash in my pockets.

9
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:01,580
I wonder if anyone will come by.

10
00:02:01,580 --> 00:02:03,380
Preferably someone to treat me.

11
00:02:03,380 --> 00:02:07,146
Next up, Nakagawa, Reiko,

12
00:02:07,196 --> 00:02:08,842
food,

13
00:02:08,892 --> 00:02:11,860
money, money, and a meal.

14
00:02:13,280 --> 00:02:14,840
It's the Chief.

15
00:02:15,860 --> 00:02:17,040
Pokémon!

16
00:02:18,460 --> 00:02:20,120
Help with the topping-out ceremony?

17
00:02:20,660 --> 00:02:24,540
That's right. Deliver the celebration gifts,
and if there's anything that needs doing, go help out.

18
00:02:24,540 --> 00:02:27,141
Wait, did you say topping-out ceremony?

19
00:02:27,191 --> 00:02:29,360
Red-and-white mochi and ohineri,

20
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:31,320
small change, but it's still money!

21
00:02:31,320 --> 00:02:34,560
Plus free sake and food!

22
00:02:35,100 --> 00:02:37,880
On top of that,
they gave us money and food as a bonus!

23
00:02:38,520 --> 00:02:38,920
What?

24
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:43,340
No, Officer Ryotsu, I'm heading
out to the topping-out celebration.

25
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:46,700
Put the celebration gifts on my tab.
I'll pay you back later.

26
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:49,960
What, you don't have any money?

27
00:02:50,980 --> 00:02:54,580
Geez, what kind of life are you living?

28
00:02:54,580 --> 00:02:55,560
I'm off.

29
00:02:56,400 --> 00:03:00,500
Listen, two bottles of celebration sake.
The brand is Otokozakari.

30
00:03:01,320 --> 00:03:02,200
Well, then.

31
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:08,340
Tch, they only gave me enough for two bottles.
How stingy.

32
00:03:10,580 --> 00:03:13,560
Right, I'm getting hungry again.

33
00:03:14,460 --> 00:03:16,320
Everyone's arriving!

34
00:03:18,580 --> 00:03:23,660
This is the money for the sake,
I can't use it, no, I really can't.

35
00:03:23,660 --> 00:03:25,800
Hic!

36
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:26,320
Argh!

37
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:36,900
Saying "What is this?", I'm already down to the last disposable chopstick.
Yeah, my survival instinct tells me to do it.

38
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:43,320
Add a tea, a croquette set meal,
and curry rice.

39
00:03:43,320 --> 00:03:47,000
No, and also potato salad and
stir-fried vegetables, aaaah!

40
00:03:50,020 --> 00:03:51,840
Ugh, that hurt.

41
00:03:52,740 --> 00:03:55,520
The money the Chief entrusted to me!

42
00:03:57,180 --> 00:04:00,400
Well, it's too late now.
I'll manage somehow.

43
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:04,180
Free food, free drinks,
just a warm-up before the meal.

44
00:04:09,680 --> 00:04:11,820
I've brought the sake as a gift.

45
00:04:12,260 --> 00:04:14,560
Excuse me,
please just set it down over there.

46
00:04:16,220 --> 00:04:17,960
Wow, what a magnificent house.

47
00:04:18,640 --> 00:04:23,220
Thanks to everyone, I've finally
got the home I've long wished for.

48
00:04:23,220 --> 00:04:26,720
Take a look at these pillars,
they're the finest cypress.

49
00:04:27,140 --> 00:04:32,040
After ten years of hardship,
this is the home I've dreamed of.

50
00:04:32,040 --> 00:04:34,060
That's truly a happy occasion.

51
00:04:34,060 --> 00:04:36,260
Well, it was worth coming
to celebrate after all.

52
00:04:36,260 --> 00:04:37,960
Ryo-san.

53
00:04:37,960 --> 00:04:42,080
Right, right, the Chief sends his regards.

54
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:45,140
Our Chief is such a tightwad, you know.

55
00:04:45,140 --> 00:04:48,520
He only gave me a little money,
so that's all I could buy.

56
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:51,480
You're too kind. Sorry for the trouble.

57
00:04:51,480 --> 00:04:57,580
Well, as you can see, today it's
packed with people, so it's crowded.

58
00:04:57,580 --> 00:04:59,220
I'll be taking my leave now.

59
00:04:59,220 --> 00:05:02,600
That's fine. Hasn't the
topping-out ceremony happened yet?

60
00:05:02,600 --> 00:05:04,520
So that's what you were after?

61
00:05:04,980 --> 00:05:08,260
It just finished a little while ago.
Too bad.

62
00:05:08,260 --> 00:05:10,580
That's not fair!
I came here looking forward to that.

63
00:05:10,580 --> 00:05:12,720
Let's do it again, okay?

64
00:05:12,720 --> 00:05:13,720
Are you serious?

65
00:05:15,140 --> 00:05:16,300
I'll head home right away.

66
00:05:16,300 --> 00:05:18,800
R-really? I'll be going home, then.

67
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:21,340
You're doing the topping-out ceremony again?

68
00:05:21,860 --> 00:05:24,520
Come on, just for show. Just a little bit.

69
00:05:24,520 --> 00:05:26,620
Everyone's already starving.

70
00:05:27,620 --> 00:05:29,960
Sorry to keep you waiting, Ryo-san.
We're starting now.

71
00:05:29,960 --> 00:05:31,380
Yes! I've been waiting for this!

72
00:05:31,380 --> 00:05:34,040
Ryo-san, you came too?

73
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:35,940
I came for the ceremony, you know.

74
00:05:36,560 --> 00:05:37,820
And the food, too, right?

75
00:05:38,020 --> 00:05:39,000
Of course!

76
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:40,540
And the free booze, too?

77
00:05:41,120 --> 00:05:42,300
It's over?

78
00:05:44,500 --> 00:05:48,160
Now, in celebration of the Yamamoto family's new home,
we will begin the topping-out ceremony.

79
00:05:48,160 --> 00:05:51,100
Been waiting! Hurry up and wrap the ohineri!

80
00:05:59,040 --> 00:06:00,600
I'm fine! I'm fine!

81
00:06:03,900 --> 00:06:04,820
This time...

82
00:06:04,820 --> 00:06:07,100
Sorry.

83
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:11,160
Hurry up,
it'd be better if you were the healthy one.

84
00:06:13,420 --> 00:06:14,460
Shaiyah!

85
00:06:15,660 --> 00:06:17,040
Wow, yay!

86
00:06:17,380 --> 00:06:19,300
A real hundred-yen coin!

87
00:06:19,300 --> 00:06:20,680
Aaaaaah!

88
00:06:22,320 --> 00:06:30,300
Ow Who's the one who put a pillar up here? Wrap it around the center,
or the house will get destroyed!

89
00:06:30,300 --> 00:06:31,340
Ōtani

90
00:06:35,040 --> 00:06:41,540
Somehow it always falls on me.
Everyone, you may take your seats now.

91
00:06:43,540 --> 00:07:04,880
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeh!

92
00:07:05,380 --> 00:07:08,560
Ryo-san, you said you'd leave
once the formalities were over.

93
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:10,540
Only Ryo-san doesn't remember

94
00:07:11,220 --> 00:07:12,460
Well, never mind.

95
00:07:12,460 --> 00:07:13,900
Today's a happy day, after all.

96
00:07:13,900 --> 00:07:15,980
Don't be so stingy, mister.

97
00:07:16,760 --> 00:07:17,820
Don't blame me.

98
00:07:19,580 --> 00:07:21,160
One at a time is too slow.

99
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:26,920
You've got quite an appetite there!

100
00:07:28,140 --> 00:07:30,080
Come on, drink up! Keep it coming!

101
00:07:30,080 --> 00:07:32,300
Alright, this way!

102
00:07:35,920 --> 00:07:57,100
Mmmmmmmmmmmmmm...

103
00:07:57,100 --> 00:07:58,700
There won't be enough
sake left for everyone!

104
00:07:58,700 --> 00:08:00,120
Don't worry about it.

105
00:08:00,120 --> 00:08:02,240
There are still two one-to barrels here!

106
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:04,860
Yeah, what a cheapskate, one barrel's gone!

107
00:08:04,860 --> 00:08:06,320
Celebrate, celebrate!

108
00:08:06,320 --> 00:08:08,440
Uh-oh, hide the sake barrels!

109
00:08:08,440 --> 00:08:10,580
No matter how many people there are,

110
00:08:10,580 --> 00:08:12,340
two to is more than enough.

111
00:08:12,340 --> 00:08:14,820
Excuse me, we've come to get some sake!

112
00:08:14,820 --> 00:08:15,160
Here I go.

113
00:08:15,160 --> 00:08:16,280
Please, please.

114
00:08:16,280 --> 00:08:18,640
Taking those would be a hassle,
so I'll take this one.

115
00:08:18,640 --> 00:08:21,920
Look, I'm on a whole different
level from ordinary people!

116
00:08:21,920 --> 00:08:22,960
That man...

117
00:08:22,960 --> 00:08:23,560
This one, this one!

118
00:08:56,780 --> 00:08:58,460
You never know what he'll pull.

119
00:08:58,460 --> 00:08:59,180
No way.

120
00:08:59,180 --> 00:09:01,740
Looks like Ryo-san's
gone off the deep end too.

121
00:09:01,740 --> 00:09:02,340
Right, right.

122
00:09:03,400 --> 00:09:06,840
Mr. Yamamoto's in for it, I'm sorry to say.

123
00:09:06,840 --> 00:09:08,040
This is serious!

124
00:09:08,040 --> 00:09:08,740
Yeah, yeah.

125
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:11,860
Cheers to the topping-out ceremony!

126
00:09:13,080 --> 00:09:14,280
Yay!

127
00:09:16,200 --> 00:09:17,380
Here it comes, here it comes!

128
00:09:17,380 --> 00:09:19,940
You really do things in a dynamic way,
don't you?

129
00:09:20,960 --> 00:09:23,000
What? What? What? What?

130
00:09:24,020 --> 00:09:43,540
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu!

131
00:09:43,540 --> 00:09:45,360
For one thing,
this house has way too many pillars.

132
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:49,160
Pillars only need one at each of the four corners.
That's plenty.

133
00:09:49,160 --> 00:09:50,560
Exactly, right?

134
00:09:51,320 --> 00:09:53,920
Alright, I'll just go on over there.

135
00:09:53,920 --> 00:09:56,100
Whoa, what are you doing?

136
00:09:56,100 --> 00:09:58,140
It's this pillar again.

137
00:09:59,140 --> 00:10:00,500
No, stop it!

138
00:10:01,700 --> 00:10:04,840
Leave the house to the carpenters.

139
00:10:04,840 --> 00:10:06,220
How can I leave it to them?

140
00:10:06,220 --> 00:10:08,380
This pillar's in the way too.

141
00:10:08,380 --> 00:10:09,100
Shall we do it?

142
00:10:09,100 --> 00:10:10,220
This one too.

143
00:10:10,220 --> 00:10:12,500
And this one as well.

144
00:10:13,540 --> 00:10:14,720
Someone stop them!

145
00:10:15,640 --> 00:10:17,320
Please stop! Master carpenter!

146
00:10:17,680 --> 00:10:19,260
What are you doing, tearing the house down!

147
00:10:19,500 --> 00:10:21,080
Do it! No, don't!

148
00:10:22,500 --> 00:10:24,460
Stay back, you lot!

149
00:10:24,580 --> 00:10:26,200
The pillar!

150
00:10:26,680 --> 00:10:28,620
Now, now, no violence!

151
00:10:28,820 --> 00:10:29,480
What did you say?!

152
00:10:30,180 --> 00:10:31,060
Complaint!

153
00:10:38,320 --> 00:10:40,040
You've really done it now!

154
00:10:40,040 --> 00:10:41,500
Ryo-san, stop it!

155
00:10:41,640 --> 00:10:43,360
Please stop, Zouldo!

156
00:10:44,540 --> 00:10:45,420
Stop!

157
00:10:52,240 --> 00:10:56,100
The makeup of my house,
built with sweat and tears,

158
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:58,620
It's the end of the world!

159
00:11:14,560 --> 00:11:15,780
Idiot!

160
00:11:18,040 --> 00:11:21,080
Don't suddenly shout like that, Chief.

161
00:11:21,080 --> 00:11:22,440
I've got a hangover, you know.

162
00:11:22,440 --> 00:11:23,900
Serves you right.

163
00:11:23,900 --> 00:11:26,560
It's because you get
carried away and go wild.

164
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:27,240
Got it?

165
00:11:27,240 --> 00:11:30,820
You're responsible for getting
the Yamamoto place back on its feet.

166
00:11:30,820 --> 00:11:31,840
Understood?

167
00:11:31,840 --> 00:11:33,320
Understood.

168
00:11:34,140 --> 00:11:36,580
Go buy me a cup of sake from Terai.

169
00:11:36,580 --> 00:11:38,560
It's a hair of the dog.

170
00:11:40,040 --> 00:11:42,020
Why is that a problem?

171
00:11:42,700 --> 00:11:43,620
Listen, Ryotsu.

172
00:11:43,620 --> 00:11:46,020
You caused trouble for other people.

173
00:11:46,020 --> 00:11:49,000
Having caused trouble,
you have to make amends.

174
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:50,420
I understand.

175
00:11:50,420 --> 00:11:51,700
So the house -

176
00:11:51,700 --> 00:11:52,400
That's right.

177
00:11:52,400 --> 00:11:53,920
But that's not enough.

178
00:11:53,920 --> 00:11:54,240
What?

179
00:11:54,240 --> 00:11:55,960
You need to reflect on your actions.

180
00:11:55,960 --> 00:11:56,980
Yes, reflecting.

181
00:11:56,980 --> 00:11:57,980
No alcohol.

182
00:11:57,980 --> 00:11:59,220
A ban on sake.

183
00:11:59,220 --> 00:12:00,160
You're teetotal from now on.

184
00:12:00,160 --> 00:12:00,640
What?

185
00:12:01,300 --> 00:12:01,700
No way.

186
00:12:02,580 --> 00:12:03,940
That's nonsense!

187
00:12:03,940 --> 00:12:08,060
I'll take responsibility for your supervisor's
discipline report by quitting drinking too.

188
00:12:08,060 --> 00:12:09,380
You're quitting too.

189
00:12:10,120 --> 00:12:13,580
If you take my sake,
what's left of me? No, no!

190
00:12:13,580 --> 00:12:15,140
No means no!

191
00:12:15,140 --> 00:12:18,420
From now on,
all alcohol is banned for one week.

192
00:12:18,420 --> 00:12:21,040
Listen, Nakagawa, Reiko, Terai.

193
00:12:21,420 --> 00:12:24,740
If you catch Ryotsu
drinking anything this week,

194
00:12:24,740 --> 00:12:26,560
go ahead and fine him on the spot!

195
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:30,420
A glass of beer, a cup of sake,

196
00:12:30,420 --> 00:12:31,900
any of them is ten thousand yen.

197
00:12:31,900 --> 00:12:34,400
Ten thousand yen?

198
00:12:34,820 --> 00:12:37,660
Chief, you don't have any money, you know.

199
00:12:37,660 --> 00:12:41,240
Don't worry. We'll write up violation
tickets and settle up on payday.

200
00:12:41,380 --> 00:12:43,066
W-what?

201
00:12:43,116 --> 00:12:45,720
A cup of sake, ten thousand yen.

202
00:12:46,820 --> 00:12:49,360
Sake, ten thousand yen. Sake.

203
00:12:55,720 --> 00:12:57,880
Well, the Chief's doing.

204
00:12:58,940 --> 00:13:02,900
Of all days, the bar signs are
catching my eye like crazy today.

205
00:13:02,900 --> 00:13:05,400
They're calling to me,

206
00:13:05,450 --> 00:13:08,000
beckoning me, "Come on, come on."

207
00:13:08,840 --> 00:13:11,920
No, I'm broke anyway.

208
00:13:11,920 --> 00:13:14,840
And the Chief confiscated all my tip money.

209
00:13:14,840 --> 00:13:18,600
Right, if I walk with my eyes closed,
I won't see the signs.

210
00:13:18,600 --> 00:13:22,080
Go, go, yes, yes, go.

211
00:13:24,540 --> 00:13:25,274
No good,

212
00:13:25,324 --> 00:13:28,660
you can't walk around
here with your eyes closed.

213
00:13:32,020 --> 00:13:33,360
Sake!

214
00:13:40,420 --> 00:13:43,640
If I gather up the little bit
left in everyone's cups over there,

215
00:13:43,640 --> 00:13:45,600
that'll make about a cupful.

216
00:13:48,880 --> 00:13:50,080
Ryotsu!

217
00:13:53,340 --> 00:13:55,640
I told you no drinking.

218
00:13:56,780 --> 00:13:58,140
C-Chief!

219
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:01,480
I know you too well.

220
00:14:01,480 --> 00:14:04,540
I knew you'd stoop to
some sneaky trick like this

221
00:14:04,540 --> 00:14:07,240
just to get your hands on some sake.

222
00:14:07,760 --> 00:14:09,540
Y-you were following me?

223
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:16,540
From now on,
I'll walk you back to the dorm every day.

224
00:14:16,540 --> 00:14:20,220
Yeah, yeah. This is so annoying.

225
00:14:22,640 --> 00:14:25,280
Crisp and refreshing,
chilled and mildly sweet.

226
00:14:25,280 --> 00:14:27,040
Master, lower pillar.

227
00:14:27,660 --> 00:14:29,060
A man's hexagonal beauty.

228
00:14:29,060 --> 00:14:29,615
Damn,

229
00:14:29,665 --> 00:14:33,300
Why do they only ever air liquor ads?

230
00:14:33,760 --> 00:14:34,900
Is Ryotsu in?

231
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:38,560
What's with that happy face, Sakonji?

232
00:14:38,560 --> 00:14:41,020
I just got a new fighting game.

233
00:14:41,020 --> 00:14:43,080
Come to my room for a sec.

234
00:14:43,080 --> 00:14:45,600
Come in, come in.

235
00:14:47,740 --> 00:14:49,640
It's really hot in here.

236
00:14:49,640 --> 00:14:51,900
Never mind, never mind. Just sit down.

237
00:14:53,720 --> 00:14:56,080
Buying a heater in this season?

238
00:14:57,040 --> 00:14:58,080
I've got a bit of a cold, you know.

239
00:14:58,080 --> 00:15:01,020
And a hot carpet too?

240
00:15:01,020 --> 00:15:02,960
Because I've got a cold, after all.

241
00:15:02,960 --> 00:15:07,020
Kotatsu too, I suppose.

242
00:15:07,700 --> 00:15:08,820
It's a game, a game!

243
00:15:08,820 --> 00:15:09,820
Pick a character.

244
00:15:14,120 --> 00:15:15,760
Yes! I won!

245
00:15:15,760 --> 00:15:18,420
If the sweat hadn't gotten into my eyes,

246
00:15:18,420 --> 00:15:19,940
I would have won, I bet.

247
00:15:21,540 --> 00:15:22,640
It's so hot.

248
00:15:22,640 --> 00:15:24,420
It's like a sauna.

249
00:15:25,300 --> 00:15:26,760
You must be thirsty.

250
00:15:28,700 --> 00:15:29,240
Just pretending.

251
00:15:35,160 --> 00:15:36,100
Ryo-chan, you're pretending!

252
00:15:36,100 --> 00:15:39,380
In this heat,
beer really is the best, isn't it?

253
00:15:39,380 --> 00:15:41,100
Hehehehe.

254
00:15:42,800 --> 00:15:43,840
No way!

255
00:15:44,540 --> 00:15:45,780
Sakonji, you!

256
00:15:46,060 --> 00:15:46,700
Eh?

257
00:15:47,700 --> 00:15:51,340
You're trying to set me up and squeeze a fine out of me,
aren't you!

258
00:15:51,900 --> 00:15:54,000
W-well, I don't know anything!

259
00:16:06,420 --> 00:16:07,620
Delicious.

260
00:16:08,980 --> 00:16:10,880
If you're not going to drink it,
I'm taking it!

261
00:16:10,880 --> 00:16:14,120
This is the last beer, you know.

262
00:16:22,160 --> 00:16:23,540
What a waste.

263
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:30,080
Game.

264
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:32,120
Beer.

265
00:16:32,860 --> 00:16:34,760
Damn it, I won't lose!

266
00:16:37,540 --> 00:16:38,600
Going home was a waste.

267
00:16:59,340 --> 00:17:00,000
Senpai

268
00:17:01,220 --> 00:17:02,180
Senpai

269
00:17:02,180 --> 00:17:05,040
I won a can of beer at pachinko, though.

270
00:17:05,040 --> 00:17:09,200
You won't trick me into
falling for your traps.

271
00:17:11,040 --> 00:17:12,000
Senpai

272
00:17:13,140 --> 00:17:15,600
Honestly, every single one of you...

273
00:17:15,600 --> 00:17:16,980
One week.

274
00:17:16,980 --> 00:17:21,040
For the next week, I won't trust anyone!

275
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:25,800
Ryo-san

276
00:17:28,440 --> 00:17:30,860
Ryo-san, come over for a bit.

277
00:17:30,860 --> 00:17:33,980
Cherry blossoms? Viewing them this late?

278
00:17:35,020 --> 00:17:38,740
These are Satsuki cherry blossoms,
and right now is their peak.

279
00:17:38,740 --> 00:17:41,140
Well, just come along,
you've got nothing to lose.

280
00:17:41,960 --> 00:17:45,780
There's top-grade sushi,
and sukiyaki with top-grade beef too!

281
00:17:46,720 --> 00:17:49,020
Well, I've got nothing better to do,
so let's take a peek.

282
00:17:51,520 --> 00:17:53,780
Whoa, this is really the real deal.

283
00:17:53,780 --> 00:17:55,760
Right? Dig in, dig in!

284
00:17:58,360 --> 00:17:58,780
Delicious!

285
00:17:58,960 --> 00:18:01,280
There's plenty more,
and we Edokko are like that too.

286
00:18:01,280 --> 00:18:03,500
Yeah, I was born in Asakusa, you know.

287
00:18:03,500 --> 00:18:06,220
What a great find, as expected of an Edokko.

288
00:18:06,220 --> 00:18:07,580
Born in Asakusa.

289
00:18:07,580 --> 00:18:09,700
Edokko always go for sushi, don't we?

290
00:18:09,700 --> 00:18:10,720
That's right.

291
00:18:10,720 --> 00:18:13,040
Sushi and sake always go together, right?

292
00:18:13,040 --> 00:18:14,100
Obviously.

293
00:18:14,100 --> 00:18:15,880
Come on, hold out your cups.

294
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:18,220
Now this one has a nice shape.

295
00:18:18,220 --> 00:18:19,800
Right? Right?

296
00:18:19,800 --> 00:18:22,620
Here it is, the finest stuff.
Look at that color.

297
00:18:22,620 --> 00:18:24,660
Mm, and the aroma is great too.

298
00:18:27,740 --> 00:18:29,440
Ryo-san, you're a true Edokko!

299
00:18:29,580 --> 00:18:30,260
Eat up!

300
00:18:30,520 --> 00:18:31,240
Drink up!

301
00:18:34,240 --> 00:18:35,540
Nice try, that won't work!

302
00:18:35,800 --> 00:18:36,700
Ryo-san!

303
00:18:38,120 --> 00:18:39,100
He got away!

304
00:18:39,440 --> 00:18:40,680
So close

305
00:18:41,160 --> 00:18:43,640
I was going to make you pay
off your tab with the fine.

306
00:18:43,640 --> 00:18:49,420
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuugh...

307
00:18:49,420 --> 00:18:50,800
So you've gone and entered
your rebellious phase.

308
00:18:51,500 --> 00:18:53,640
But today's exactly one week, you know.

309
00:18:53,640 --> 00:18:54,340
Not yet.

310
00:18:54,340 --> 00:18:56,620
We need you to defy the Chief.

311
00:18:56,620 --> 00:18:57,580
Defy him, you mean?

312
00:18:59,420 --> 00:19:00,860
Finally, it's over.

313
00:19:00,860 --> 00:19:02,300
You held out well, didn't you.

314
00:19:02,840 --> 00:19:03,540
How about it, Ryotsu?

315
00:19:03,540 --> 00:19:06,460
How about we use this as a chance
to quit drinking completely?

316
00:19:06,460 --> 00:19:08,260
You've got to be kidding.

317
00:19:08,260 --> 00:19:10,620
Let's go for a drink on
the way back from the temple.

318
00:19:10,620 --> 00:19:11,260
But...

319
00:19:12,020 --> 00:19:14,440
Sorry, but we've got work tonight.

320
00:19:14,880 --> 00:19:17,300
It's for the Takepon
Kingdom's ambassador to Japan's

321
00:19:17,300 --> 00:19:19,060
goodwill reception. We're on security duty.

322
00:19:24,340 --> 00:19:26,380
Any suspicious characters around?

323
00:19:26,380 --> 00:19:28,680
No, nothing unusual.

324
00:19:29,500 --> 00:19:33,440
No suspicious people,
but there's a suspicious drink...

325
00:19:33,440 --> 00:19:33,740
Senpai.

326
00:19:33,740 --> 00:19:34,180
Yocchan.

327
00:19:38,360 --> 00:19:41,180
What? Why are only you
two dressed like that?

328
00:19:41,600 --> 00:19:45,700
Reiko-san and I were personally
invited to this party.

329
00:19:46,240 --> 00:19:47,180
That's right.

330
00:19:47,180 --> 00:19:53,220
Then it's unfair that only you two get to
eat and drink this luxurious feast for free.

331
00:19:53,920 --> 00:19:54,960
Nakagawa, switch with me.

332
00:19:56,140 --> 00:19:57,500
Reiko will do, too.

333
00:19:57,500 --> 00:19:59,220
Then do you want to wear my dress?

334
00:20:00,120 --> 00:20:03,200
Well, we'll go make a round then.

335
00:20:03,740 --> 00:20:05,980
We'll keep watch properly, so don't worry.

336
00:20:07,980 --> 00:20:11,760
Right in front of us, all that free food
and drink is just swarming, and yet...

337
00:20:21,100 --> 00:20:22,760
Damn, so close.

338
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:26,100
This time for sure.

339
00:20:36,220 --> 00:20:37,760
Did something happen?

340
00:20:38,400 --> 00:20:42,020
A growl like some wild beast
came from under the table.

341
00:20:48,440 --> 00:20:50,200
Nothing in particular.

342
00:20:52,440 --> 00:20:53,880
That's strange.

343
00:20:56,140 --> 00:20:58,460
Ladies and gentlemen, esteemed guests,

344
00:20:58,460 --> 00:21:01,400
now, the host of tonight's party,

345
00:21:01,400 --> 00:21:04,840
the Ambassador of the Kingdom of Takepon,
will hold a bouquet toss.

346
00:21:04,840 --> 00:21:08,300
If you think you have what it takes,
please come up and catch the bouquet.

347
00:21:15,040 --> 00:21:16,700
It's our traditional bouquet toss!

348
00:21:17,180 --> 00:21:19,200
Reiko, why don't you join in?

349
00:21:19,820 --> 00:21:24,180
It would be nice if they said whoever
catches the bouquet gets married next, but...

350
00:21:24,180 --> 00:21:30,020
whoever catches this bouquet has to have a drinking contest with the ambassador,
after all.

351
00:21:30,020 --> 00:21:31,360
Senpai.

352
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:36,080
What, what?
I'm being pushed out more and more!

353
00:21:36,080 --> 00:21:37,580
One, two, three!

354
00:21:45,100 --> 00:21:48,600
Yes, you there, please come this way.

355
00:21:52,560 --> 00:21:53,980
It's the senior.

356
00:21:55,100 --> 00:21:56,460
A bad feeling.

357
00:21:57,980 --> 00:21:59,140
No.

358
00:21:59,140 --> 00:22:00,900
Hello, hello.

359
00:22:00,900 --> 00:22:03,860
Would you prefer a plant, or sake?

360
00:22:03,860 --> 00:22:06,240
I'm whatever you like, desu-gozaru.

361
00:22:07,580 --> 00:22:09,540
Sake? You can drink sake?

362
00:22:09,800 --> 00:22:11,740
It's a drinking contest with me.

363
00:22:12,120 --> 00:22:13,280
Yahoo!

364
00:22:15,840 --> 00:22:19,400
N-no way! I today I'm a bit...

365
00:22:20,880 --> 00:22:22,740
You can't refuse, senpai.

366
00:22:22,740 --> 00:22:24,080
That's right, Ryo-chan.

367
00:22:24,560 --> 00:22:26,320
Well, why is that?

368
00:22:26,320 --> 00:22:30,480
At the Takepon Kingdom ceremony,
you caught the bouquet, didn't you?

369
00:22:30,480 --> 00:22:33,800
Turning down a drink is
the worst insult there is.

370
00:22:34,220 --> 00:22:37,560
That's not good, it could develop
into an international incident.

371
00:22:37,560 --> 00:22:41,000
Ryotsu, it's fine,
accept it so you don't offend anyone.

372
00:22:41,500 --> 00:22:42,220
Really?

373
00:22:44,920 --> 00:22:47,220
Ryotsu, you may drink.

374
00:22:47,220 --> 00:22:49,830
Good! You may drink, but...

375
00:22:49,880 --> 00:22:52,540
Just don't go overboard!

376
00:23:02,980 --> 00:23:03,900
The floor! The floor!

377
00:23:05,320 --> 00:23:07,120
The ceiling's spinning?

378
00:23:07,520 --> 00:23:10,160
What? The ceiling's spinning?

379
00:23:10,360 --> 00:23:13,500
No! No! The floor's shaking!

380
00:23:21,860 --> 00:23:23,740
Right, I'll fix it.

381
00:23:23,740 --> 00:23:27,180
Fun, fun! I'll help too!

382
00:23:27,180 --> 00:23:32,160
My pillar's tilting too!

383
00:23:32,160 --> 00:23:34,680
Alright, here I come, I'll fix everything!

384
00:23:37,080 --> 00:23:38,240
Next, over here.

385
00:23:38,980 --> 00:23:41,140
Then, I... I'll do it myself.

386
00:23:42,460 --> 00:23:44,440
Alright, last one, here we go!

387
00:24:18,300 --> 00:24:20,620
Thinking back on the time after the rain

388
00:24:21,740 --> 00:24:24,560
as I walked, looking back

389
00:24:24,560 --> 00:24:27,200
holding Mom's hand

390
00:24:28,260 --> 00:24:30,400
the feeling I had back then

391
00:24:31,440 --> 00:24:34,400
was a strange feeling

392
00:24:34,400 --> 00:24:35,840
So

393
00:24:35,840 --> 00:24:39,600
on the arcade guide tiles,

394
00:24:39,600 --> 00:24:45,280
I tried walking only on the black parts

395
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:53,520
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone forgets

396
00:24:54,680 --> 00:25:01,000
Politicians with their pompous faces,
and the aunties who are a thorn in your side

397
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:06,580
Turn that corner over there

398
00:25:07,660 --> 00:25:11,720
You can meet everyone, everyone

399
00:25:14,280 --> 00:25:16,440
Over there, there's a wall

400
00:25:17,640 --> 00:25:19,740
Well, I'm sure there's a wall

401
00:25:21,240 --> 00:25:24,980
Everybody, come on over to our town

402
00:25:26,100 --> 00:25:26,500
Thank you

403
00:25:29,220 --> 00:25:31,500
Damn! Those who aren't streamlined!

404
00:25:31,660 --> 00:25:34,500
Even though they're just editors,
they go around in helicopters!

405
00:25:34,500 --> 00:25:35,440
They're popular with women!

406
00:25:35,440 --> 00:25:38,460
They can eat all the good food they want,
so I'm so jealous!

407
00:25:38,460 --> 00:25:41,860
That's it, I'll be an editor beyond editors,

408
00:25:41,860 --> 00:25:44,260
I'll become a Super Editor!

409
00:25:44,260 --> 00:25:47,860
Look forward to Super
Editor next time, okay?

410
00:25:48,700 --> 00:25:50,920
Over there is Kameary!

411
00:25:51,920 --> 00:25:54,660
Well, surely it's Kameary!

412
00:25:55,600 --> 00:25:59,300
Everyone, come on over to our town!

413
00:26:00,400 --> 00:26:00,840
Thank you!

